Subject: [PATCH] virtio-snd: pace capture startup and own converters before cancellation

On an M4 MacBook Pro, PipeWire entered an approximately 100 Hz capture
PREPARE/START/STOP/RELEASE loop. The CoreAudio input callback received no
frames, while caulk::audio_buffer_resource grew continuously. Playback-only
and no-sound runs remained stable.

The input pump completed all queued descriptors even before PCM_START, and
also delivered unpaced silence while the asynchronous microphone worker
opened its unit. This advances the guest capture hw_ptr outside its running
interval or much faster than the sample clock, triggering ALSA XRUN recovery.

Only pump capture during START. Wait for the opening worker, wake the pump
when its unit is published, and pace silence at the guest rate if no input
device can be opened. Initialize callback frame size/channels for device
Float32 (not the guest format). Own AudioConverter immediately so failures
and stop_pending cancellation after initialization dispose it too.

Regression tests use real guest descriptors without opening a microphone:
no completion before START/while opening/after STOP, and clock-paced U8
fallback silence. Both new regressions fail with the original pump.

